  <body>
    <script>document.documentElement.classList.add('js');</script>
    <div class="shell">
      <nav class="nav"><a class="brand" href="#top">Global Health Signals</a><div class="navlinks"><a href="#question">Question</a><a href="#data">Data</a><a href="#model">Model</a><a href="#residuals">Residuals</a><a href="#brief">Brief</a></div></nav>
      <main id="top">
        <section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow reveal">WHO GHO Data / TabPFN / Health Intelligence</p><h1 class="reveal">From public health data to <em>predictive evidence.</em></h1><div class="hero-grid reveal"><p class="lead" id="heroLead">Can public health indicators from WHO explain and predict differences in life expectancy across countries?</p><div class="note-card"><p>This report converts heterogeneous WHO country-year indicators into a modeling layer, then asks whether a tabular foundation model can recover a meaningful life-expectancy signal. The value is not only the score: the residuals show where countries depart from the pattern expected by the available data.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">WHO GHO API</span><span class="tag">Life expectancy</span><span class="tag">TabPFN</span><span class="tag">Prior Labs</span><span class="tag">Interactive residuals</span></div></div></div><div id="loadNotice"></div></div></section>

        <section class="section" id="question"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="chapter">00 / Analytical architecture</span><div><h2>A country-year prediction problem, not a generic dashboard.</h2><p class="section-copy">The unit of analysis is a country in a year. The target is life expectancy at birth. The features are mortality, immunization, expenditure, disease and data-quality indicators from WHO. The purpose is to test signal strength, benchmark model performance and identify records that deserve policy-context follow-up.</p></div></div><div class="flow reveal"><div class="flow-step"><small>01</small><strong>Acquire</strong><span>Pull public indicators from the WHO GHO OData API.</span></div><div class="flow-step"><small>02</small><strong>Structure</strong><span>Convert indicators into a country-year analytical table.</span></div><div class="flow-step"><small>03</small><strong>Audit</strong><span>Measure coverage, missingness and modeling readiness.</span></div><div class="flow-step"><small>04</small><strong>Model</strong><span>Compare Ridge, Random Forest and TabPFN on a temporal split.</span></div><div class="flow-step"><small>05</small><strong>Interpret</strong><span>Use residuals to find countries above or below expected outcomes.</span></div></div></section>

        <section class="section" id="data"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="chapter">01 / Data foundation</span><div><h2>The dataset is global, but not equally complete.</h2><p class="section-copy">The first analytical decision is to keep data quality visible. Coverage is not just a preprocessing concern: it changes how much confidence we should place in cross-country comparisons and helps explain why some regions or countries are harder to model.</p></div></div><div class="metrics reveal" id="datasetMetrics"></div><div class="grid2 reveal"><div class="panel"><div class="panel-pad"><h3>Variable coverage profile</h3><p class="explain">Click a row to inspect coverage. Higher coverage means the indicator appears in more country-year rows and is more stable for cross-country modeling.</p><div class="viz-layout"><div class="viz-list" id="coverageBars"></div><aside class="detail" id="coverageDetail"></aside></div></div></div><div class="panel"><div class="panel-pad"><h3>Completeness by WHO region</h3><p class="explain">Click a region to inspect its average data completeness. This is a governance signal, not a performance ranking.</p><div class="viz-layout"><div class="viz-list" id="regionCompleteness"></div><aside class="detail" id="completenessDetail"></aside></div></div></div></div></section>

        <section class="section" id="model"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="chapter">02 / Model benchmark</span><div><h2>TabPFN is the only model below one year of average error.</h2><p class="section-copy">The split is temporal: records before 2015 train the models, and records from 2015 onward test them. This prevents the report from only measuring fit on historical data and makes the result closer to a forward-looking evaluation.</p></div></div><div class="panel reveal"><div class="story"><div><h3>Executive reading</h3><p><b>MAE</b> is the average absolute difference between predicted and observed life expectancy. A value of 0.94 means the TabPFN estimate missed the observed outcome by less than one year on average.</p><p><b>R²</b> measures explained variation. TabPFN reached 0.96 on the recent test set, compared with 0.88 for Random Forest and 0.76 for Ridge.</p><p>The comparison matters because it shows the gain is not simply a product of the dataset. The tabular foundation model extracts more usable structure from the same input table.</p></div><div><div class="model-stack" id="modelComparison"></div></div></div></div></section>

        <section class="section" id="residuals"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="chapter">03 / Residual intelligence</span><div><h2>The error layer is where the report becomes investigative.</h2><p class="section-copy">Residuals are calculated as observed minus predicted life expectancy. Positive residuals indicate performance above the model expectation; negative residuals indicate outcomes below what the available indicators suggested. These are not labels of success or failure. They are leads for deeper analysis.</p></div></div><div class="findings reveal" id="findingCards"></div><div class="grid2 reveal" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="panel"><div class="panel-pad"><h3>Regional model difficulty</h3><p class="explain">Click a region to compare mean absolute prediction error. Higher error suggests the model needs more local context.</p><div class="viz-layout"><div class="viz-list" id="regionResiduals"></div><aside class="detail" id="residualDetail"></aside></div></div></div><div class="panel"><div class="panel-pad"><h3>Temporal stress point</h3><p class="explain">Hover the points. Error rises in 2021, suggesting a stress period where mortality patterns shifted faster than the selected features could summarize.</p><svg class="line-chart" id="yearResiduals" viewBox="0 0 600 320"></svg></div></div></div></section>

        <section class="section" id="brief"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="chapter">04 / Intelligence brief</span><div><h2>What the first version already supports.</h2><p class="section-copy">The first result supports a concise executive conclusion: WHO indicators contain predictive signal for life expectancy, TabPFN improves the benchmark, and the most valuable next layer is a country-level residual investigation.</p></div></div><div class="brief-grid reveal"><article class="brief"><h3>Conclusion</h3><p>Public health indicators can estimate recent life expectancy with high accuracy when structured as a country-year tabular problem.</p></article><article class="brief"><h3>Risk</h3><p>Data completeness remains uneven. Any executive use of the model should keep the coverage layer visible beside predictions.</p></article><article class="brief"><h3>Next analysis</h3><p>Eswatini, Kuwait 2021 and high-error regional clusters should become case cards with local context and indicator trajectories.</p></article></div><div class="panel reveal" style="margin-top:14px"><div class="panel-pad"><h3>Highest-error country profiles</h3><p class="explain">Click a card to inspect the case. A high error can reflect a true shock, missing variables, country-specific dynamics, or indicator lag.</p></div><div class="case-grid" id="countryCases"></div></div></section>
      </main>
      <footer class="footer">Built from WHO Global Health Observatory data. Modeling layer: Prior Labs / TabPFN. Repository: who-global-health-signals.</footer>
    </div>
    <div class="tooltip" id="tooltip"></div>
    <script type="module">
      const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);
      const fmt = n => Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 2 });
      const pct = n => `${Math.round(Number(n) * 100)}%`;
      const labelName = s => String(s ?? '').replaceAll('_',' ').replace(/\b\w/g,c=>c.toUpperCase());
      const load = async name => { const r = await fetch(`/data/${name}.json`, { cache:'no-store' }); if(!r.ok) throw new Error(`Could not load /data/${name}.json (${r.status})`); return r.json(); };
      const tip = $('tooltip');
      function showTip(html,e){tip.innerHTML=html;tip.style.left=`${e.clientX}px`;tip.style.top=`${e.clientY}px`;tip.style.opacity=1}
      function hideTip(){tip.style.opacity=0}
      function setDetail(el,kicker,title,body,value){el.innerHTML=`<span class="kicker">${kicker}</span><span class="big">${value}</span><p><b>${title}</b><br>${body}</p><div class="hint">Click rows to update</div>`}
      function interactiveBars({el,detail,data,label,value,max=null,formatter=fmt,detailText}){const vals=data.map(d=>Number(d[value])||0);const m=max??Math.max(...vals,.01);el.innerHTML=data.map((d,i)=>`<div class="viz-item ${i===0?'active':''}" role="button" tabindex="0" data-index="${i}"><div class="viz-top"><span class="viz-label">${labelName(d[label])}</span><span class="viz-value">${formatter(Number(d[value])||0)}</span></div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:${Math.max(3,((Number(d[value])||0)/m)*100)}%"></div></div></div>`).join('');const update=i=>{const d=data[i];el.querySelectorAll('.viz-item').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('active',Number(x.dataset.index)===i));setDetail(detail,'Selected signal',labelName(d[label]),detailText(d),formatter(Number(d[value])||0))};el.querySelectorAll('.viz-item').forEach(item=>{item.addEventListener('click',()=>update(Number(item.dataset.index)));item.addEventListener('mousemove',e=>{const d=data[Number(item.dataset.index)];showTip(`<strong>${labelName(d[label])}</strong>${detailText(d)}`,e)});item.addEventListener('mouseleave',hideTip)});update(0)}
      function drawYearLine(svg,data){const w=600,h=320,m={top:28,right:28,bottom:42,left:52};const years=data.map(d=>Number(d.year));const vals=data.map(d=>Number(d.mean_abs_error));const minX=Math.min(...years),maxX=Math.max(...years),maxY=Math.max(...vals)*1.18;const sx=x=>m.left+((x-minX)/Math.max(1,maxX-minX))*(w-m.left-m.right);const sy=y=>h-m.bottom-(y/Math.max(.01,maxY))*(h-m.top-m.bottom);const pts=data.map(d=>`${sx(Number(d.year))},${sy(Number(d.mean_abs_error))}`).join(' ');const xTicks=[...new Set(years)].filter((_,i)=>i%2===0);const yTicks=[0,maxY/2,maxY];svg.innerHTML=`<rect x="0" y="0" width="600" height="320" fill="rgba(255,255,255,.012)" rx="18"/>${yTicks.map(t=>`<line x1="${m.left}" y1="${sy(t)}" x2="${w-m.right}" y2="${sy(t)}" stroke="rgba(247,243,232,.08)"/><text x="${m.left-8}" y="${sy(t)+4}" fill="#9d958b" font-size="10" text-anchor="end">${fmt(t)}</text>`).join('')}<line x1="${m.left}" y1="${h-m.bottom}" x2="${w-m.right}" y2="${h-m.bottom}" stroke="rgba(247,243,232,.18)"/><line x1="${m.left}" y1="${m.top}" x2="${m.left}" y2="${h-m.bottom}" stroke="rgba(247,243,232,.18)"/>${xTicks.map(t=>`<text x="${sx(t)}" y="${h-14}" fill="#9d958b" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle">${t}</text>`).join('')}<polyline points="${pts}" fill="none" stroke="#d7ff6f" stroke-width="2.6"/>${data.map((d,i)=>`<g class="year-point" data-index="${i}" style="cursor:pointer"><circle cx="${sx(Number(d.year))}" cy="${sy(Number(d.mean_abs_error))}" r="13" fill="rgba(215,255,111,.08)"/><circle cx="${sx(Number(d.year))}" cy="${sy(Number(d.mean_abs_error))}" r="4.8" fill="#f7f3e8"/></g>`).join('')}`;svg.querySelectorAll('.year-point').forEach(g=>{g.addEventListener('mousemove',e=>{const d=data[Number(g.dataset.index)];showTip(`<strong>${d.year}</strong>Mean error: ${fmt(d.mean_abs_error)} years<br>Countries: ${fmt(d.countries)}`,e)});g.addEventListener('mouseleave',hideTip)})}
      function showError(error){console.error(error);$('loadNotice').innerHTML=`<div class="notice"><strong>Data assets did not load.</strong><br>Run <code>python scripts/11_export_report_assets.py</code> and <code>python scripts/12_prepare_web_assets.py</code>, then restart <code>npm.cmd run dev</code>. Details: ${error.message}</div>`;document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el=>el.classList.add('in'))}
      async function main(){try{const [summary,models,regionRes,yearRes,countryRes,completeness,coverage]=await Promise.all(['report_summary','model_comparison','region_residuals','year_residuals','country_residuals_top','data_completeness_by_region','variable_coverage'].map(load));$('heroLead').textContent=summary.analytical_question;$('datasetMetrics').innerHTML=`<div class="metric"><span class="num">${fmt(summary.dataset.full_rows)}</span><span class="label">country-year rows</span></div><div class="metric"><span class="num">${fmt(summary.dataset.countries)}</span><span class="label">countries/entities</span></div><div class="metric"><span class="num">${summary.dataset.min_year}–${summary.dataset.max_year}</span><span class="label">historical range</span></div><div class="metric"><span class="num">${fmt(summary.best_model.test_mae)}</span><span class="label">TabPFN MAE years</span></div>`;interactiveBars({el:$('coverageBars'),detail:$('coverageDetail'),data:coverage.slice(0,10),label:'variable_name',value:'non_null_share',max:1,formatter:pct,detailText:d=>`Coverage in the country-year table: ${pct(d.non_null_share)}. Missing share: ${pct(d.missing_share)}.`});interactiveBars({el:$('regionCompleteness'),detail:$('completenessDetail'),data:completeness,label:'region',value:'mean_completeness',formatter:pct,detailText:d=>`Average data completeness: ${pct(d.mean_completeness)} across ${fmt(d.countries)} countries and ${fmt(d.rows)} country-year rows.`});const maxMae=Math.max(...models.map(m=>Number(m.test_mae)));$('modelComparison').innerHTML=models.map((m,i)=>`<article class="model-row" data-index="${i}"><div><strong>${labelName(m.model)}</strong><small>${fmt(m.test_rows)} recent test rows</small></div><div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:${Math.max(5,(1-Number(m.test_mae)/maxMae)*82+18)}%"></div></div><p class="model-note">RMSE ${fmt(m.test_rmse)} · R² ${fmt(m.test_r2)}</p></div><div class="model-score"><span class="num">${fmt(m.test_mae)}</span><small>MAE years</small></div></article>`).join('');$('modelComparison').querySelectorAll('.model-row').forEach(row=>row.addEventListener('mousemove',e=>{const m=models[Number(row.dataset.index)];showTip(`<strong>${labelName(m.model)}</strong>MAE ${fmt(m.test_mae)} years<br>RMSE ${fmt(m.test_rmse)}<br>R² ${fmt(m.test_r2)}`,e)}));$('modelComparison').addEventListener('mouseleave',hideTip);const picks=['overall_error','best_region','worst_region','worst_year','positive_outlier','negative_outlier'];$('findingCards').innerHTML=summary.executive_findings.filter(d=>picks.includes(d.finding_id)).map(d=>`<article class="finding"><strong>${typeof d.value==='number'?fmt(d.value):d.value}</strong><p><b>${d.metric}</b><br>${d.finding}</p></article>`).join('');interactiveBars({el:$('regionResiduals'),detail:$('residualDetail'),data:regionRes.sort((a,b)=>Number(a.mean_abs_error)-Number(b.mean_abs_error)),label:'region',value:'mean_abs_error',formatter:fmt,detailText:d=>`Mean absolute prediction error: ${fmt(d.mean_abs_error)} years. Rows: ${fmt(d.rows)}. Countries: ${fmt(d.countries)}.`});drawYearLine($('yearResiduals'),yearRes);$('countryCases').innerHTML=countryRes.slice(0,10).map((d,i)=>`<article class="case-card" data-index="${i}"><span class="rank">#${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><strong>${d.country_code}</strong><span>${d.region??'Unknown region'}</span><div class="case-metric"><span>mean error</span><b>${fmt(d.mean_abs_error)}</b></div><div class="case-metric"><span>residual</span><b>${fmt(d.mean_residual)}</b></div></article>`).join('');$('countryCases').querySelectorAll('.case-card').forEach(card=>card.addEventListener('click',()=>{$('countryCases').querySelectorAll('.case-card').forEach(c=>c.classList.remove('active'));card.classList.add('active')}));const obs=new IntersectionObserver(entries=>entries.forEach(e=>{if(e.isIntersecting)e.target.classList.add('in')}),{threshold:.12});document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el=>obs.observe(el));setTimeout(()=>document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el=>el.classList.add('in')),400)}catch(error){showError(error)}}main();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
